{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: in the wrap-up report written after Artroom is built, include a short section on Cloudflare K2 (https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-k2-streams/) as a future direction: a post-commit exporter that sends each sealed log entry to a K2 stream, so many outside consumers (dashboards, chat bridges, search, mirrors, audit) and an organisation-wide feed across rooms read from one stream instead of holding cursors on each Room Durable Object. Design rule: K2 carries copies, never authority. The exporter follows the notify pattern (R-LOG-13), with no external I/O during admission. Consumers skip duplicates by ActId, detect gaps from seq and refill with log({ after }), and verify signatures against the published log. Note what K2 is not for: sequencing, fencing or live updates (about 1 s p99 produce latency, at-least-once delivery, 7-day default retention, beta limits). Out of scope for the contest build.","body":{"conditions":"The wrap-up report on main has a section that describes the K2 entry exporter as future work, states the rule that K2 carries copies and never authority, and lists the limits that keep K2 out of sequencing and live updates.","target_head":"ca61351fc3a886760b2b7d1d11e241a05b38550e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}